## Summary
This pull request refines captioning behavior for HTML 5 video tracks and allows an implementing developer to selectively ignore supplementing canvases that may not be intended for closed captioning/subtitling. A new configuration option of `ignoreCaptionLabels` provides an array of string values that will filter and ignore rendering of the `<track/>`. To make things even cleaner, the `<track/>` element is now a `<Track/>` sub component.

## Testing
Test by filtering tracks to the matching label of the annotation resource.

### Example:
`
const options: any = {
  ignoreCaptionLabels: ["Chapters"],
};
`

Where the annotation intended to ignore has the structure:
```
{
  "id": "http://127.0.0.1:8080/fixtures/iiif/manifests/captions.json/canvas/1/page/annotation_page/1/annotation/2",
  "type": "Annotation",
  "motivation": "supplementing",
  "body": {
    "id": "http://127.0.0.1:8080/fixtures/vtt/around_the_corner_chapters.vtt",
    "type": "Text",
    "format": "text/vtt",
    "label": {
      "en": ["Chapters"]
    },
    "language": "en"
  },
  "target": "http://127.0.0.1:8080/fixtures/iiif/manifests/captions.json/canvas/1"
}
```

## Note
While completing local testing, I did not that captioning was not working in Mozilla Firefox Developer edition. It does seem to work in all major browsers including the consumer level firefox.

